\section{Sampling}{

Chains are run in parallel by default. Set \code{options(mc.cores = 1)} (or pass
\code{cores = 1}) on shared servers, in containers, or inside another parallel
context.

The sampler runs with \code{adapt_delta = 0.95} by default, which reduces
divergences at the cost of slightly longer runtime. Override it, or set any
other sampler control, by passing a \code{control} list through \code{...}, for example
\code{control = list(adapt_delta = 0.99)}; only the entries supplied are changed.
See the \code{control} argument of \code{\link[rstan:stan]{rstan::stan()}} for the full set of entries.

Check convergence with \code{\link[=kb_converged]{kb_converged()}}, \code{\link[=glance]{glance()}}, or \code{\link[=summary]{summary()}}.
}

\section{Site and year interaction}{

The site:year effect lets each site depart from the year-to-year pattern
shared by all sites, so a site can have a good year while others have a poor
one. Separating it from the site and year effects needs at least one site
surveyed in more than one year and at least one year with more than one
site. Without that, as with data from a single year, the fit warns:
estimates for the surveyed site-years are unaffected, but the site or year
effects, and predictions for other site-years or new sites and years, depend
on the \code{sd_site_year} prior. Use \code{\link[=kb_sensitivity]{kb_sensitivity()}} to check how much they
do.
}

